export anchor SectionedReportStyle:
    number: 195
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Sectioned report
    idea: The home screen reads as a numbered status report on a white sheet, with large light section numerals in the margin and a sticky contents list on the left, so the week can be read top to bottom or jumped to by section.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #eef0f3, the page behind the sheet and the contents rail
        sheet: #ffffff, the report sheet, the header and fields
        ink: #16202e, text, the heavy rules and the nav band
        muted: #4f5b6b, labels, refs and meta
        rule: #d5dae1, row hairlines, never text
        navy: #1f3a68, the primary button, the current nav item, the this week line and focus
        navyTint: #e6ebf3, initials and the focused row
        numeral: #5a6b8c, the large section numerals and the last week line
        green: #1e6b45, On track with a check in a circle
        amber: #8f4f00, At risk with a bang in a triangle
        red: #a3222b, Behind with a cross in an octagon and overdue figures
    type:
        One sans stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans,
        system-ui, with ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas for refs.
        Section numerals are 56px light at minus 0.04em, the greeting 40px
        bold at minus 0.02em, summary figures 44px light tabular, section
        titles 22px bold, body 15px at 1.55, refs 12px mono and table
        labels 11px bold caps tracked 0.1em.
    layout:
        A white header row holds a navy square B mark with the brand, a
        square search field, a navy New project button, a square bell with
        a red count and an initials square with Mara Okafor. Beneath it a
        full width ink band carries six caps nav links with Home filled
        navy. The body is a 220px contents rail and a white report sheet on
        the grey desk. The rail has a Contents label, a numbered list of
        Summary, Projects, Needs attention, Throughput and Activity with a
        3px navy edge on the current item, and a note that the report is
        for the week ending 31 Oct and prepared for Mara Okafor. It stays
        sticky while the sheet scrolls. The sheet opens with a caps
        eyebrow, the greeting and a lede that starts with the red overdue
        clause, closed by a 3px ink rule. Each section is a two column row
        with a large light numeral under a 3px navy cap in a 72px margin,
        and a heading under a 1px ink rule. Section 1 shows the four
        figures in a row split by thin rules. Section 2 is a ledger table
        with refs 2.1 to 2.6, team, status, percent with an outlined meter,
        tasks and due, and a total row. Section 3 lists numbered findings
        for the overdue tasks and the two troubled projects with derived
        remaining tasks and target pace. Section 4 overlays this week as a
        solid navy line with dots on last week as a dashed line with
        squares, beside a totals list. Section 5 is a when, who and what
        log. Below 1080px the contents become a horizontal tab row above
        the sheet, and on phones numerals sit above headings and the
        ledger scrolls inside its own frame.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px above each section, 56px sheet padding and 24px between numeral and text.
    density: Medium. Reading pace, with one idea per numbered section.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: A 3px ink rule under the report head, a 3px navy cap over each numeral, 1px ink over each heading and ledger head, and 1px grey between rows.
    shadows: None. The white sheet sits on the grey desk with a 1px border.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.5px with square caps. Status is an outline check
        circle, bang triangle or crossed octagon beside its word, and
        overdue uses a clock.
    focus: A solid 2px navy outline offset 2px with a white gap ring, and a navy tint on a focused ledger row.
    tone: Report voice with refs, such as 3.2 Billing migration, Total and Change.
